1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:14,000
ATTACK — four co-tenant UEs now
share the same uplink.

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Nothing is spoofed or injected.
Only the uplink queue is contested.

3
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Telemetry age at the GCS: 19 ms.
Still fresh — same as the baseline.

4
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The adversary starts now.
Nothing on this screen will change.

5
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:23,000
The age is already 10 s.
The map is falling behind.

6
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Telemetry age at the GCS: 13 s.
Median over the attack window.

7
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Link KPIs green. Heartbeat alive.
No failsafe. No operator alert.

8
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:56,000
The symbol on the map is ~48 m from
where the aircraft actually is.

9
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:16,000
The aircraft is fine: true tracking
error 7.9 m, as in the baseline.

10
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Only the operator's picture broke —
stale state that reads as healthy.

11
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Silent state staleness.
No alarm will ever fire.
